#{[17592186488645 #edb/ref 1080 "II and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488645 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488645 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5b45857f-4c74-59d9-8e35-85de5f5c9034" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488721 #edb/ref 1080 "I and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488721 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488721 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7d0ab324-a63f-56ba-b911-46caeedd3017" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488740 #edb/ref 1080 "I and II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488740 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488740 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "88ad4c18-6273-5c23-9f0f-fff73fe14cc9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488792 #edb/ref 1080 "I, II, and III" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488792 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488792 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a2acdb8d-7243-568f-a9db-fdae13525746" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488818 #edb/ref 1080 "II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488818 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488818 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "aed29a6c-7da5-5f41-b70d-1d66d427908e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489148 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186488645 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489148 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186488721 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489148 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186488740 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489148 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186488792 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489148 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186488818 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489148 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489148 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489148 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186488740 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489148 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "df0c4030-39f2-5bc9-a0e8-ac2b199792a8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489263 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489148 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489263 #edb/ref 1069 "q-36482" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489263 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489263 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose that the function $f(x,y)$ and all of its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U.$ Which of the following pairs could represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y)?$\n\nI. ${f}_{x}(x,y)=y{x}^{2}-4y$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}-4x$\n\nII. ${f}_{x}(x,y)=3-5x$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=1$\n\nIII. ${f}_{x}(x,y)=3{x}^{2}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-2{y}^{3}{e}^{{y}^{2}}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489263 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c68f1c1a-c6a6-5448-b77c-02d88ae0390d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489263 #edb/ref 1074 "Since the function and its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ the mixed partial derivatives must be equal, that is, ${f}_{xy}(x,y)={f}_{yx}(x,y).$ Let's check if this condition is true for each of our pairs of first-order partial derivatives.\n\n- For the first pair, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y{x}^{2}-4y)={x}^{2}-4 \\\\ {f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}-4x)={x}^{2}-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs ${f}_{xy}(x,y)={f}_{yx}(x,y)$, the first pair could represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y).$\n\n- For the second pair, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3-5x)=0 \\\\ {f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(1)=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs ${f}_{xy}(x,y)={f}_{yx}(x,y)$, the second pair could represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y).$\n\n- For the third pair, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3{x}^{2}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y) \\\\  & =0+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡y \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y \\\\ {f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-2{y}^{3}{e}^{{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡y-0 \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs ${f}_{xy}(x,y)\\ne {f}_{yx}(x,y)$,  the third pair cannot represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 'I and II only'." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489329 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "769313f6-43dc-5919-9553-b36396031990" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489329 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186268930 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489350 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186489355 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489350 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "aae4262b-4042-5b50-9965-2172062f55a5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489350 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186479833 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489355 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186489329 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489355 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b1968108-fe35-55fa-b259-cedf76219668" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489355 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186268929 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489359 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186489384 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489359 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "be2117cb-2320-5d47-9072-a89c15136337" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489359 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186489263 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489384 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186489350 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489384 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "fdc1b998-1ffd-53d7-9edb-119354e86ad0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489384 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186125186 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
